; A top-level `let`, then a top-level `defn` that reads it. Three sibling kernels
; close over the binding and answer 107; the runtime refuses the name at compile.
; The same shape ONE frame deeper — a let inside a defn body, read by a defn declared
; in that body — agrees everywhere. So the divergence is the top-level frame alone.
;
; Authored as .fk because it has to run on kernels with no BML front end; see
; observe/fixtures/intern-order-seal-first.fk for the same reason stated in full.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(do
    (let outer 7)
    (defn sees-outer () outer)
    (add 100 (sees-outer)))
